# Release integrity artifacts are byte-exact: checksums are computed and
# signatures are made over the working-tree bytes, so autocrlf smudging on a
# branch switch must never rewrite them. The v1.1.23 publish shipped
# CRLF-mangled copies of every tracked text asset because a post-signing
# branch switch re-smudged the working tree and the upload followed it;
# the published-set signature verification caught it. These rules pin the
# working tree to the committed bytes for the release surfaces.
release/SHA256SUMS_*.txt -text
release/RELEASE_NOTES_*.md -text
release/VALIDATION_REPORT_*.md -text
release/zmeta-release-manifest.yaml -text
*.asc -text
